Hrm, that's an odd statement.  I'm sure many inexperienced players have
never even thought of save-scumming (either that, or I'm horridly
unimaginative, since it didn't occur to me until I saw it in RGRN's FAQ),
and I'd be willing to bet that a decent number play on public servers, and
don't have access to the saves directory.

Of course, that's all moot, since David's point as I read it is that most
players have a lot of experience with the early-game challenges, and are
able to experiment fairly freely to find a solution, since, if they die,
they haven't lost much playing time.  The late-game challenges, however,
don't encourage experimentation, since you have to struggle just to reach
them.  This gives a severe benefit to the spoiled player, since they don't
have to die the first time they meet Orcus just to find out he's carrying
that wand, and then die again to him to determine that he always carries it,
etc., etc.

If you make the late-game challenges hard for spoiled players, then the
un-spoiled most likely won't have a chance.



